12.8.4 D. Debugging Post-Mortem: Top 3 Chapter 12 Failure Modes

Shared Mutable Class Attributes (patients = [] Outside __init__): Declaring a list or dict at the class body level makes every instance silently share one memory container. Always create mutable state inside __init__ (self.patients = []).
Re-Fitting Inside .transform() (Silent Data Leakage): Computing min(values), max(values), or mean inside .transform() instead of reusing self.min_, self.max_, or self.mean_ breaks the fundamental train/test boundary in machine learning.
Forgetting self. When Reading or Writing Attributes: Writing mean_ = sum(valid) / len(valid) inside .fit() creates a temporary local variable that vanishes as soon as .fit() returns, leaving self.mean_ permanently stuck at None!








